But the problem was, after you UUdecoded NH308PC1.UU to get NH308PC1.EXE, it
gave you and error, and NH308PC1.EXE wouldn't extract files when it was run.
That's why I had to use PKZipFix on it.  I didn't use the INSTALL.BAT file
because I prefer to "do it myself".  I just peeked at it and see what they did
and they did it myself.

NH308PC1.UU is _bad_ on Linc.  It's missing the last byte on the UUencode
stream.  So, it makes a bad Zip file that whines when you run it.  PKZipFix
fixs it so it will run.

